0,Malaryan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malaryan_language,"Malaryan (Mala Arayan, Malayarayar, IPA: [mɐlɐrjɐn]) is an extinct Dravidian language of Kerala and Tamil Nadu that was closely related to Malayalam.",Malaryan,Dravidian
1,Dravidian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dravidian_peoples,"The Dravidian peoples, Dravidian-speakers or Dravidians, are a collection of ethnolinguistic groups native to South Asia who speak Dravidian languages. There are around 250 million native speakers of Dravidian languages. [1]",Malaryan,Dravidian
