3,dravidian dithyramb (ttbb) (pdf if ordered for entire choir),https://earthsongschoralmusic.com/product/m-24/,"The Dravidian Dithyramb embodies traces of ragas from the Carnatic music of South India, but it also bears an astonishing resemblence to the tarana - a form of Hindustani classical music which uses Persian and Arabic phonemes as nonsense syllables. See also S-42: satb and S-179: ssaa; satb version recorded on cd-02. Notable for its",Malaryan,Dravidian
4,The Indigenous Music of Kerala 'Sopana Sangeetham ',https://anandfoundation.com/indigenous-music-kerala-sopana-sangeetham/,Chapter Two highlights the Evolution of Sopana Music. Sopana Sangeetham is a continuation of Dravidian music. The period of Dravidian music is from the Sanghom period to the rule of the Cheras (4 AD to 10 AD).,Malaryan,Dravidian
